        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cheung Kong Center, Hong Kong, Beaconsfield House\n- Events: A Symphony of Lights\n- Organizations: Information Services Department\n\nFacts:\n- Beaconsfield House was built in 1963.\n- Beaconsfield House housed the Information Services Department until 1995.\n- In 1995, Beaconsfield House and the neighboring Hong Kong Hilton were demolished to make way for the Cheung Kong Center.\n- Cheung Kong Center is a building in Hong Kong.\n- Cheung Kong Center has coloured lights on its sides that illuminate at night in intricate light shows, which is common in Hong Kong.\n- A Symphony of Lights is a daily light and sound show in Hong Kong.",
